{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The proposed development is located within surface water\r\nflood zones 3a high &amp;amp; 3b medium. In the absence of a satisfactory Flood\r\nRisk Assessment, it has not been demonstrated that the proposed development\r\nwould not exacerbate the risk of flooding within the site or increase the risk\r\nand consequences of flooding elsewhere, contrary to National Planning Policy\r\nFramework (2024), Policy SI 12 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CSU of\r\nthe Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policies DM9 and DM10 of the Harrow Development\r\nManagement Policies Local Plan (2013) and Policy CN4 of the Draft New Local\r\nPlan (2021-2041) (Regulation 19 Version).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The applicant has failed to provide sufficient technical evidence to demonstrate that the development would achieve an acceptable standard of fire safety. This is of particular concern given the proposal’s location beneath the flyover spanning George Gange Way bridge, and the potential risk regarding the spread of fire, a critical risk to the highway network. In the absence of detailed modelling, the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that a fire would not compromise the structural integrity of the flyover, thereby posing a significant risk to highway users. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy D12 of the London Plan (2021), Policy DM44 of the Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and Policy GR3B of the Draft New Local Plan (2021-2041) (Regulation 19 Version).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
